# Database

## Supabase + PostgreSQL

All schema changes are managed through Supabase migrations. Migrations are the source of truth; never mutate the schema directly in the dashboard in production.

## Timestamps

- Use `timestamptz` for all timestamp columns. Store in UTC — never with a local offset.
- Standard audit columns: `created_at timestamptz not null default now()` and `updated_at timestamptz not null default now()`.
- See `date-time.mdc` for how timestamps are handled in application code.

## Naming

- Tables: `snake_case`, plural (e.g. `lead_activities`).
- Columns: `snake_case` in English.
- Foreign keys: `<noun>_id` (e.g. `lead_id`, `assigned_sdr_id`).

## Row Level Security

Enable RLS on every table. Write explicit policies; do not rely on the absence of a policy to restrict access.

## Types

Until `supabase gen types` is part of the workflow, describe row shapes in `lib/` (e.g. `LeadRecord`). Do not invent a parallel database client or untyped `any` rows.

## Query access

Access the database only through the Supabase client helpers in `lib/supabase/`. Do not instantiate `@supabase/supabase-js` directly outside that module.
